  "bridges": [
    {
      "before_panel": 1,
      "text": "Dad and Daughter frame a warning comic: how economic fear, antisemitic lies, and propaganda helped Nazis destroy democracy from inside, then run a genocide machine. Panels rotate through Hitler\u2019s hate mythology, Goebbels\u2019s media craft, a Weimar voter\u2019s craving for order, a neighbor\u2019s bystander silence, Eichmann\u2019s paperwork cruelty, a Jewish teen\u2019s stolen childhood, Himmler\u2019s terror state, and resistance courage\u2014each  Night study. A history book open between them. The lesson is a warning, not a spectacle."
    },
    {
      "before_panel": 2,
      "text": "Early 1930s Germany: unemployment lines, worthless savings stories, and politicians selling rage as strength."
    },
    {
      "before_panel": 3,
      "text": "Hitler sells a fake story of national rebirth built on racial hierarchy and conspiracy fantasies."
    },
    {
      "before_panel": 4,
      "text": "Daughter names the trick before it hardens into 'common sense.'"
    },
    {
      "before_panel": 5,
      "text": "1933: appointed Chancellor; emergency powers and the Enabling Act hollow out the republic. Opposition vanishes into prisons and camps."
    },
    {
      "before_panel": 6,
      "text": "Gleichschaltung: press, radio, film, and schools pulled into one loud story. Book burnings teach fear of questions."
    },
    {
      "before_panel": 7,
      "text": "Dad maps the craft to modern pattern language\u2014without inventing private crimes about living leaders."
    },
    {
      "before_panel": 8,
      "text": "Nuremberg Laws: citizenship and dignity cut away with paperwork and badges of exclusion."
    },
    {
      "before_panel": 9,
      "text": "Kristallnacht: broken glass in the street\u2014public violence taught as normal."
    },
    {
      "before_panel": 10,
      "text": "Terror as policy: secret police, camps for opponents, a racial-purity cult wearing uniforms of order."
    },
    {
      "before_panel": 11,
      "text": "War accelerates genocide. Deportations become timetables. Murder hides inside logistics language."
    },
    {
      "before_panel": 12,
      "text": "Dad names the history Hannah Arendt later helped the world confront: the banality of evil."
    },
    {
      "before_panel": 13,
      "text": "A White Rose echo: students risk everything so truth can still circulate in the dark."
    },
    {
      "before_panel": 14,
      "text": "Aftermath classroom: institutions matter\u2014and so do habits of courage."
    },
    {
      "before_panel": 15,
      "text": "They translate history into present civic radar\u2014patterns, not conspiracy fan-fiction about living politicians."
    },
    {
      "before_panel": 16,
      "text": "Close the book\u2014not the duty."
    }
  ]
